   "id": "guaranteed_returns",
   "title": "Why promised returns matter",
   "body": "SEBI's guide to spotting scams says to be suspicious of anyone who promises assured or near-certain returns, because all securities market investments carry some degree of risk. SEBI's investor website also says registered investment advisers are prohibited from guaranteeing returns. When a message promises a fixed or daily return, the promise itself is what to look at, not the sender's story. Ruko can't vouch for any tip, app or person.",
